  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SEA Risk Management: Transforming Collective Action for an Effective PSEA Response (Phase II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Given the large ongoing complex humanitarian crisis within country, Mozambique and Philippines were selected as pilot countries for this project with the objective to reduce the risk of sexual exploitation and abuse within crisis&#x2010;affected communities through a collective SEA risk management approach which leads to strengthened PSEA responses within country. Additionally, sustainable collective SEA risk management models will be identified and integrated within pilot countries and shared with global PSEA and other fora to promote replication in other contexts.</narrative>
  </description>
